# .mailmap — canonical author identities.
#
# git log/shortlog/blame and GitHub's contributor attribution all honour this
# file, so a wrong identity in an already-published commit is correctable WITHOUT
# rewriting history. That matters here: both `main` branches are force-push
# protected (GitLab "not allowed to force push to a protected branch", GitHub
# GH006), so a rewrite would require lifting a control that exists for good reason.
#
# The mapping below covers commits 334ea2d and 1b8346d (2026-08-19). Their author
# was set to a TEST FIXTURE identity because a coordinator diagnostic exported
# GIT_DIR at the real repository while the test suite ran: makeRepo()-style helpers
# in tests/ call `git config user.email/user.name` without an explicit target, so
# the fixture identity landed in this repo's local .git/config. Content and review
# of both commits are unaffected — only the author line was wrong.
#
# Keeping the mapping permanently is deliberate: it also neutralises any FUTURE
# recurrence of the same fixture identity, which is cheaper than detecting it late.
Bernhard Götzendorfer <208284447+Kanevry@users.noreply.github.com> Test <test@example.com>
